# Test: ze doctor --json accepts an mcp server entry that names no port
# VALIDATES: the SECOND operator surface. `ze config validate` and `ze doctor`
# reach MCP validation through different code -- cmd_validate.go builds its own
# result, config.ValidateSemantics feeds the doctor bridge -- so a config the one
# accepts and the other rejects is how an operator gets contradictory answers
# about the same file. Both read the 8080 the schema promises.
# PREVENTS: doctor rejecting the config an operator writes from the YANG.
#
# Owner ruling 2026-08-23: extractMCPBlock applies `refine port { default 8080; }`
# rather than the YANG dropping it. This file asserted the refusal until then.
#
# The listener probe itself is not asserted here: it binds 127.0.0.1:8080, so
# whether it reports doctor-listen-unavailable depends on what else holds that
# port on the machine running the test. The extraction and the probe endpoint are
# pinned together by TestListenerDefaultsAgreeWithMCPExtraction
# (internal/component/config/listener_test.go), which needs no free port.
#
# Sibling: test/parse/mcp-listener-port-default.ci covers `ze config validate`,
# and test/parse/mcp-listener-port-default-disabled.ci covers the switched-off
# block that starts nothing.

tmpfs=mcp-port-default.conf:terminator=EOF_CONF
environment {
    mcp {
        enabled true
        server primary {
            ip 127.0.0.1
        }
    }
}
EOF_CONF

cmd=foreground:seq=1:exec=ze doctor --json mcp-port-default.conf
# The positive assertion first: doctor ran and produced its report. Without it a
# doctor that printed nothing at all would satisfy the absence below.
expect=stdout:contains="schema-version": 1
expect=stdout:!contains=config-mcp-invalid
